<div><p>RE: Public Records Request REQUEST of July 26, 2026., Reference # R=
000911-072626.</p><p>Dear Robert Samuel White,</p><p>In accordance with ORS=
 192.324(2), this acknowledges our receipt of your July 26, 2026, public re=
cords request. Your request included the following:</p><p><strong>&quot;To =
the Public Records Officer, Department of Administrative Services:<br><br>T=
his is a request under ORS 192.311 to 192.478. I am also giving notice of m=
y intent to petition the Attorney General regarding two prior requests, add=
ressed at the end of this message.<br><br>I am Robert Samuel White, date of=
 birth April 11, 1977. I served as a volunteer with the Oregon Parks and Re=
creation Department at Jessie M. Honeyman Memorial State Park in February a=
nd March 2025. I was dismissed on March 24, 2025, and permanently excluded =
from all OPRD volunteer programs on March 26, 2025, in a letter citing my p=
ublic comments about staff. On March 24, 2026, Oregon State Police and a Un=
ited States Forest Service special agent were sent to my residence on restr=
icted federal land.<br><br>I request the following records for the period F=
ebruary 1, 2025 to the present, except as otherwise specified.<br><br>1. Al=
l records concerning me held by DAS in any division, including the Chief Hu=
man Resources Office, Risk Management, Enterprise Goods and Services, and t=
he Office of the Director. This includes records indexed under Robert White=
, Robert Samuel White, Robert S. White, Sam White, or my date of birth.<br>=
<br>2. All records reflecting any behavioral threat assessment, threat mana=
gement, workplace violence assessment, or safety planning process concernin=
g me. This includes but is not limited to: workplace violence incident repo=
rts; reports made under Statewide HR Policy 50.010.02; threat assessment te=
am or workplace violence prevention team records, agendas, minutes, notes, =
or referrals; completed or partial assessment instruments of any kind; desi=
gnations of me as a subject of concern, person of concern, or equivalent; s=
afety plans; no-contact or no-trespass directives; and any recommendation t=
o contact or involve law enforcement.<br><br>3. All communications between =
DAS and OPRD concerning me, including any consultation, guidance, or techni=
cal assistance provided by DAS to OPRD regarding my dismissal, my exclusion=
, my correspondence, my public records requests, the archive at oprdvolunte=
erabuse.org, or the March 24, 2026 police visit.<br><br>4. All communicatio=
ns between DAS and Oregon State Police, the Oregon Department of Justice, t=
he Office of the Governor, or any federal agency concerning me.<br><br>5. A=
ll records reflecting the disclosure of my personal information, including =
my date of birth, my residence, or my volunteer file, to any person or agen=
cy outside OPRD.<br><br>6. The following policy and training records, witho=
ut regard to date:<br><br>(a) Statewide Policy 50.010.02, Violence-Free Wor=
kplace, in both the version effective 11/1/2024 and the superseded version =
effective 02/01/2019.<br><br>(b) Statewide Policy 50.010.04, Workplace Effe=
cts of Domestic Violence, Sexual Assault, and Stalking, and the accompanyin=
g online Toolkit referenced in 50.010.02(4).<br><br>(c) The DAS-CHRO Violen=
ce and Weapons Free Workplace training required by 50.010.02(10), including=
 all slides, scripts, scenarios, handouts, and completion records.<br><br>(=
d) Any agency safety plan, procedure, guidance, form, checklist, or assessm=
ent instrument used to carry out 50.010.02(4) or 50.010.02(6), including an=
y used to assess reported incidents, and any addressing application of the =
policy to volunteers or other non-employees within the definition of &quot;=
others working in an agency.&quot;<br><br>(e) Any guidance, training, or wr=
itten material issued by DAS or CHRO to executive branch agencies concernin=
g behavioral threat assessment, threat management teams, or workplace viole=
nce prevention teams.<br><br>(f) Any record identifying the agency director=
s, human resource sections, or safety sections designated to administer 50.=
010.02 at the Oregon Parks and Recreation Department, and any delegation of=
 that authority. <br><br>7. All records reflecting the number of behavioral=
 threat assessments, workplace violence assessments, or threat management p=
rocesses initiated by executive branch agencies since January 1, 2023, in w=
hatever aggregate or summary form DAS maintains.<br><br>If any responsive r=
ecord is withheld, please identify it by date, author, recipient, and subje=
ct, and cite the specific exemption claimed. If DAS is not the custodian of=
 a particular record, please identify the custodian rather than closing the=
 request. ORS 192.311(2)(b) defines the custodian to include a public body =
that owns or retains a record, and DAS is the custodian of its own correspo=
ndence.<br><br>I request a fee waiver. Disclosure of these records is in th=
e public interest. The question of whether an authority created to prevent =
violence has been used against a volunteer for documenting his own treatmen=
t is a matter of public concern, and the resulting records bear on the cond=
uct of two state agencies toward a member of the public.<br><br>Notice rega=
rding two prior requests: I intend to petition the Attorney General under O=
RS 192.411 concerning requests R000879 and R000885, which DAS has not resol=
ved in a manner consistent with its obligations under ORS 192.311 to 192.47=
8. That petition will be filed this week and published with its exhibits.<b=
r><br>I have an active public records petition before the Attorney General =
concerning Oregon State Police, PR27478, and I have given notice of intent =
to file a claim under ORS 30.275 concerning the March 24, 2026 police visit=
. Please treat all records identified above as subject to litigation hold.<=
br><br>Robert Samuel White<br>rsw@rswfire.com<br>PO Box 334, Reedsport, OR =
97467<br>https://oprdvolunteerabuse.org&quot;</strong></p><p>The Oregon Dep=
artment of Administrative Services is the custodian of some of these record=
s but is unsure if it=E2=80=99s the custodian of some of the requested reco=
